From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Domenico D'Arrigo <DCHEM88@hotmail.it>
Date: Sat, 31 Oct 2026 02:42:45 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] northbridge/intel/haswell: Timestamps around the native RAM
 init

The mrc.bin path records TS_INITRAM_START and TS_INITRAM_END around
sdram_initialize() (haswell_mrc/raminit.c), the native RAM init records
nothing. cbmem -t then has no RAM init entry on a native RAM init build,
and tools that time it see only the whole romstage: on the W541 the
MEM-01 check of hw-report.py skips ("nessun timestamp della RAM init"),
and BOOT-02 cannot take a training boot, up to a minute, out of the boot
time. Record the same two timestamps around do_actual_raminit(), which
covers the training on a cold boot and the restore from the cache on a
fast boot or an S3 resume.

The span is not the same work as mrc.bin's. early_init_native() runs
before it: the wait for the ME UMA in intel_early_me_init() (up to 1 s),
the CPU replacement check on a cold boot (up to 50 ms), and the early
PCH and DMI init of the native path. The mrc.bin path calls none of
them, so whatever mrc.bin does in their place falls inside its span.
RAM init figures of the two variants are not to be compared one to one.

The pre-RAM entries go into the CAR timestamp table, which mrc.bin
builds fill with the same two entries, so the table needs no more room.
The change is in the shared northbridge and also gives the T440p these
entries.

TEST=Host syntax check with -Werror and the ci-150 W541 nri config.
Still to test on the W541 (nri): cbmem -t lists "before RAM
initialization" and "after RAM initialization" on a training boot, a
fast boot and an S3 resume, and hw-report.py reports MEM-01 instead of
skipping it; the time from the start of romstage to "before RAM
initialization" shows what early_init_native() costs.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 .../intel/haswell/native_raminit/raminit_native.c            | 5 +++++
 1 file changed, 5 insertions(+)

diff --git a/src/northbridge/intel/haswell/native_raminit/raminit_native.c b/src/northbridge/intel/haswell/native_raminit/raminit_native.c
index 019606ebad..06aef201af 100644
--- a/src/northbridge/intel/haswell/native_raminit/raminit_native.c
+++ b/src/northbridge/intel/haswell/native_raminit/raminit_native.c
@@ -12,6 +12,7 @@
 #include <northbridge/intel/haswell/raminit.h>
 #include <southbridge/intel/lynxpoint/me.h>
 #include <southbridge/intel/lynxpoint/pch.h>
+#include <timestamp.h>
 #include <types.h>
 
 #include "raminit_native.h"
@@ -181,9 +182,13 @@ void perform_raminit(const bool s3resume)
 	wait_txt_clear();
 	wrmsr(0x2e6, (msr_t) {.lo = 0, .hi = 0});
 
+	timestamp_add_now(TS_INITRAM_START);
+
 	const enum raminit_boot_mode bootmode =
 			do_actual_raminit(s3resume, cpu_replaced, orig_bootmode);
 
+	timestamp_add_now(TS_INITRAM_END);
+
 	report_memory_config();
 
 	if (intel_early_me_uma_size() > 0) {
